			<title>Madonna's W.E. Official Trailer doing justice to the movie. First good comments from the press</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/154-madonnas-we-official-trailer-doing-justice-to-the-movie-first-good-comments-from-the-press.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/154-madonnas-we-official-trailer-doing-justice-to-the-movie-first-good-comments-from-the-press.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>The official trailer of <strong>W.E.</strong> is doing justice to the movie directed by <strong>Madonna</strong>. A few minutes were enough to make general public and some media open up their eyes and realize that critics were factious and specious.</p>
<p>The second <strong>Madonna</strong>'s fatigue had a never-ending standing ovation in Venice at the end of the screening gala, but press omitted to report it.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>"The movie may have received mixed reviews, but when the very first trailer debuted online this morning, we must admit we were pleasantly surprised," writes <a href="http://www.marieclaire.co.uk/news/celebrity/531813/watch-madonna-s-w-e-trailer.html" target="_blank" title="Marie Claire Madonna W.E.">Marie Claire</a>. "Stunningly beautiful and uber-stylish, we'll certianly be first in line to see this one," they add.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>"The trailer shows a beautiful cinematography by <strong>Hagen Bogdanski</strong>," <a href="http://www.aceshowbiz.com/news/view/00044476.html" target="_blank" title="Aceshowbiz Madonna W.E.">AceShowbiz</a> reports.</p></div>]]></description>
