		<item>
			<title>Madonna's W.E. to be released in UK cinemas on January 12, 2012</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/140-madonnas-we-to-be-released-in-uk-cinemas-on-january-12-2012.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/140-madonnas-we-to-be-released-in-uk-cinemas-on-january-12-2012.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>The <strong>UK</strong> release date for <strong>Madonna</strong>'s second directoral film <strong>W.E.</strong> has been finally announced today.</p>
<p><strong>W.E.</strong> will open in <strong>UK</strong> cinemas on <strong>January 12, 2012</strong>. As we earlier reported, the movie will be distributed in the Great Britain by <strong>StudioCanal</strong>.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>Don't forget that W.E. will get its UK premiere at <strong>BFI London Film Festival</strong> on October 23. The gala screening will take place at <strong>London Empire Leicester Square</strong>. <strong>BFI</strong> told DrownedMadonna.com that <strong>Madonna</strong> is expected to attend the premiere, but "guests lists for <strong>London Film Festival</strong> events are not 100% confirmed until the day of the event and are even at that point subject the change."</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>Movies</category>
			<pubDate>Thu, 06 Oct 2011 21:21:55 +0000</pubDate>
