		<item>
			<title>Oscar Isaac on Madonna and the W.E. Premiere at the Venice Film Festival</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/134-oscar-isaac-on-madonna-and-the-we-premiere-at-the-venice-film-festival.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/134-oscar-isaac-on-madonna-and-the-we-premiere-at-the-venice-film-festival.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>Interviewed by <a href="http://www.theatermania.com/off-broadway/news/10-2011/oscar-isaac-here-and-now_41787.html" target="_blank" title="Theater Mania">Theater  Mania</a>, <strong>W.E.</strong> actor <strong>Oscar Isaac</strong> talks about <strong>Madonna</strong> and the premiere of <strong>W.E.</strong> in <strong>Venice</strong> for the Film Festival.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>"It  was great. I had never been to <strong>Venice</strong>," says <strong>Oscar</strong>. "The  Italians and <strong>Madonna</strong> are really a cool mix, and it was great to  see the film for the first time with such a warm audience."</p>
<p><strong>Oscar</strong> also talks about having <strong>Madonna</strong> as a director. "She was intense, she was really determined, and she has an amazing  wealth of knowledge about art and aesthetics, so it was easy to trust  her," he says. "What's really great about her is that she expects the best of  everyone and won't settle for mediocrity. I had to learn to play piano  for this role, and she made sure I went to rehearsal every day."</p>
<p>"I found  it refreshing to work with someone who's into every minute detail," <strong>Oscar</strong> adds.</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>Interviews</category>
			<pubDate>Tue, 04 Oct 2011 11:48:11 +0000</pubDate>
