		<item>
			<title>Madonna's W.E. Vionnet installation at Harvey Nichols London: Photographs of the Showcasing</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/124-madonnas-we-vionnet-installation-at-harvey-nichols-london-photographs-of-the-showcasing.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/124-madonnas-we-vionnet-installation-at-harvey-nichols-london-photographs-of-the-showcasing.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>A few days ago we reported about the exclusive <strong>Vionnet</strong> installation at <strong>Harvey Nichols London</strong>, showcasing specially commisioned pieces by <strong>Vionnet</strong> from the film <strong>W.E.</strong></p>
<p> </p>
<p>We can finally show you a few photographs of the installations thanks to <strong>Harvey Nichols London</strong> and <strong>Vionnet Paris</strong>. Enjoy!</p>
<p> </p>
<p><img src="http://drownedmadonna.com/img/2011/harvey-nichols/01.jpg" border="0" alt="W.E. Vionnet Harvey Nicholson London" width="790" height="1053" style="border: 0;" /></p>
<p><img src="http://drownedmadonna.com/img/2011/harvey-nichols/02.jpg" border="0" alt="W.E. Vionnet Harvey Nicholson London" width="790" style="border: 0;" /></p>
<p><img src="http://drownedmadonna.com/img/2011/harvey-nichols/03.jpg" border="0" alt="W.E. Vionnet Harvey Nicholson London" width="790" style="border: 0;" /></p>
<p><img src="http://drownedmadonna.com/img/2011/harvey-nichols/04.jpg" border="0" alt="W.E. Vionnet Harvey Nicholson London" width="790" style="border: 0;" /></p>
<p> </p>
<p><strong>Harvey Nichols London</strong> is hosting the special Vionnet installation till September 30 in a dedicated space on the First Floor of the store. The installation is providing customers with the unique opportunity to view the special archive pieces from the film.</p>
<p>"<strong>Harvey Nichols</strong> is the perfect place to showcase the intricate and exquisite pieces and will allow customers to truly appreciate the attention to detail and craftsmanship of the House"   explains <strong>Matteo Marzotto</strong>, CEO of <strong>Vionnet</strong>.   <strong>Vionnet</strong> worked alongside director Madonna and costume designer <strong>Arianne Phillips</strong> to re-create original <strong>Vionnet</strong> pieces from <strong>Wallis Simpsons</strong> wardrobe.</p>
<p>The installation is providing customers with a greater awareness of the unique heritage and vision of <strong>Madeleine Vionnet</strong>.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>Vionnet Installation,</p>
<p>14th- 30th September 2011</p>
<p>Harvey Nichols,</p>
<p>Knightsbridge London,</p>
<p>SW1X 7RJ</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>Movies</category>
			<pubDate>Mon, 26 Sep 2011 14:11:42 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Harvey Nichols showcasing Vionnet pieces worn in Madonna's W.E.</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/115-harvey-nichols-showcasing-vionnet-pieces-worn-in-madonnas-we.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/115-harvey-nichols-showcasing-vionnet-pieces-worn-in-madonnas-we.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p><strong>London's Harvey Nichols</strong> is showcasing a selection of <strong>Vionnet</strong> pieces worn in <strong>Madonna</strong>'s second director fatigue, <strong>W.E.</strong>, as seen on <strong>Andrea Riseborough</strong>.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>"The film <strong>W.E.</strong> gave <strong>Vionnet</strong> such a wonderful opportunity to showcase the exquisite craftsmanship and skill of the house," the label's ceo <strong>Matteo Marzotto</strong> told <strong>Vogue</strong>. "We were thrilled to be considered for the project and it was so exciting to be part of such a lavish production that portrayed one of history's most intriguing women.  The film, <strong>W.E.</strong>, challenged us to utilise our extensive knowledge and craftsmanship to re-create the original pieces designed by <strong>Madeleine Vionnet</strong> for <strong>Wallis Simpson</strong> with precision and accuracy. Extensive research was carried out on fabrics and construction using original pieces from the archives at the Louvre."</p>
<p> </p>
<p>The chosen pieces will be shown on <strong>London's Harvey Nichols</strong>' first floor, alongside the current autumn/winter 2011-12 collection.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>"<strong>Harvey Nichols</strong> is such a visionary retailer with a world renowned reputation so it is such a pleasure that <strong>Vionnet</strong> can work with them on this installation," said <strong>Marzotto</strong>. "The store is the perfect place to showcase the intricate and exquisite pieces and will allow customers to truly appreciate the attention to detail and craftsmanship of the house, we hope that the installation provides a greater awareness of the unique heritage and vision of <strong>Madeleine Vionnet</strong>."</p>
<p> </p>
<p>The installation will be on display until Friday September 30.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>109 - 125 Knightsbridge</p>
<p>London</p>
<p>SW1X 7RJ</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>Movies</category>
			<pubDate>Fri, 23 Sep 2011 11:30:10 +0000</pubDate>
